{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened","id":125314,"title":"Uratha Origins ,what exactly happened ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-04T13:18:22-07:00","id":125314,"title":"Uratha Origins ,what exactly happened ?","content":"Ok we know the story , Mama Moona had her way with Papa Lupo and made the ... um I think this is not exactly clear . What exactly came of this union ?<br /> <br /> <b>a)The first born ?</b><br /> If this is the case then the first born are the first werewolves and not just wolf spirits , probably they were the first shapeshifting wolf spirits , but could they be the first werewolves as well ?<br /> Were the first born the actual fathers-mothers of the first Uratha ?<br /> <br /> <b>b)The first werewolves themselves?</b><br /> In this case who birthed the first born ? And when father wolf died why some of them had to go against their mother ?<br /> If Luna is not their mother then why to bother withe litter of their father's bastards ?<br /> The first born of the pure tribes should hate them because they are offsptings of the moon bitch and not accept them at all .<br /> <br /> What do you think about this guys and gals ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T13:41:14-07:00","id":125332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened#post125314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think about this guys and gals ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Firstborn are the cousins of the first werewolves, according to common Uratha lore. The Great Wolf-God progenitor of the species had the Firstborn through other powerful wolf-spirits.<br /> <br /> The First Pack are the first werewolves, who gave rise to the rest of the Uratha on a timeline that is not entirely clear relative to the Sundering. Some of them decided to kill and replace their ailing parent, and went on to become the first of the Forsaken. Others neglected to or failed to stop the Forsaken from carrying out the murder of their progenitor and became the Pure some time after they shared in the punishment of their brethren.<br /> <br /> Dire Wolf hates the Uratha for the destruction of his paradise. Rabid Wolf may be utterly mad, and fears for his safety as the omega of the pack the Firstborn ran as; now that that pack has been divided by their adopted children's feud, he cleaves to what he believes to be the strongest side - the one with the Wolf's oldest, strongest, bitterest child on it alongside the powerful monsters of the Shadow. Silver Wolf values purity and sees Luna's failure to protect hir consort as a betrayal of the highest order.<br /> <br /> It is probably not accidental that the Firstborn and the First Pack suffer a great deal of narrative confusion between each other in the telling of their stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T13:58:08-07:00","id":125343,"title":"","content":"I'm by no means an expert, but I think you need to brush up on your Uratha mythology. Now, obviously Uratha culture is so steeped in symbolism and metaphor that you cannot take any of this literally. However, this is the story as The People tell it. Father Wolf and Mother Luna were the parents of the firstborn, and for a long time they were the apex predators of Pangea. Then one day, Father Wolf failed in a hunt. The Azlu and the Bieshlu are the remnants of the spirits that were able to escape Father Wolf in his old age. This was proof that he was no longer fit to lead the pack, and had to be put down to avoid becoming a burden to those who were still strong enough to hunt. The firstborn of the Forsaken tribes were the ones who did what they knew had to be done for the good of the pack, while the firstborn of the Pure tribes were the ones who wanted to let their father live. Father Wolf's death sundered Pangea and creates separate worlds of spirit and flesh, but the werewolves became what they are now, walkers in both worlds but belonging to neither. The Pure hate the Uratha because the killed their ancestral father, not because they're the offspring of Luna. In fact, both are Luna's children, but for what ever reason, she seems to favor her patricidal children. Presumably because they were willing to sacrifice their own honor for the good of the pack, and though she was angry at them at first she has come to realize it was the right choice. As for if they are the literal biological ancestors of all modern werewolves? Maybe. Or maybe it's just a story. To The People, it really doesn't make much difference. What matters is the lesson that the myth teaches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T16:12:21-07:00","id":125376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened#post125314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok we know the story ,</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is just as likely complete and utter bunk. To paraphrase one of the WoD writers a long time ago, &quot;Never trust a story that starts off saying that it is true.&quot;<br /> <br /> Its like the Genesis story. Full of symbolism, but few people take it literally. Werewolves were born of a union of wolf spirits and human flesh, granted balance and raised in light of the moon. The &quot;Father&quot; gives them purpose and duty, while the &quot;Mother&quot; grants them love, life, and feeds them.<br /> <br /> If it was a literal story, then Moon/Wolf's children should have been hybrid spirits, no flesh involved. Clearly, since the Uratha are half human, the story is full of errors and woefully incomplete. You can pretty much fill in the plot holes however you want, depending of the needs of your individual game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T16:16:57-07:00","id":125379,"title":"","content":"Also, First Born aren't werewolves. Those are the names for the Werewolf Totems. Fenrir-Ur and the rest. They are the first children of Father Wolf, before the birth of the Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T16:53:08-07:00","id":125398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=125376#post125376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If it was a literal story, then Moon/Wolf's children should have been hybrid spirits, no flesh involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf the Forsaken Core Rulebook, Chapter 1, Shadow History - The Tale of Pangaea, p22</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Pangaea was in full bloom, its beauty seduced the heart of the moon itself. Mother Luna \u2014 Amahan Iduth \u2014 grew enchanted with the world growing beneath her. <b>She took the form of a woman of flesh and descended to earth.</b> She walked among the jungles and swam in the seas. She was the most beautiful creature in the world, and she had countless suitors. The greatest and most valiant was Urfarah\u2026 and you know that name, don\u2019t you? He was Father Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Clearly, since the Uratha are half human, the story is full of errors and woefully incomplete. </div> </div> </div>Or, y'know, it's a story involving <i>gods</i> who pretty much by definition play fast and loose with the rules of the setting even before invoking the &quot;in a time when the world was different and things could be done that no longer work&quot; trope. The Uratha can already point to the Hosts as evidence that spirits-made-flesh are a thing that can happen.<br /> <br /> There are less artless ways to point out that myths are myths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T17:13:18-07:00","id":125401,"title":"","content":"The Uratha Origin so far is something blurry ! Another fact is that Uratha breed only with flesh humans , not even wolves (not as a core rule to the least) , also when two werewolves produce offsprings these creatures are not flesh stuff (about to change in IC) , perhaps not spirits either since they tend to be miasma to the spirit world since they are immune to it . Another fact is that Uratha cannot breed with spirits , actually even spirits may not breed with spirits , but I have heard some stories that Pure First born tried to Rape ? female spirits who now are tied to the forsaken . Probably things change dramaticaly for spirits beyond the 6th level . But for a wolf spirit to produce half human offsprings ? Especially shapeshifting half human offsprings . maybe the ''birth'' case was a completely different procedure that we possibly can imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T17:26:18-07:00","id":125408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=125398#post125398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026<br /> Or, y'know, it's a story involving <i>gods</i> who pretty much by definition play fast and loose with the rules of the setting even before invoking the &quot;in a time when the world was different and things could be done that no longer work&quot; trope. The Uratha can already point to the Hosts as evidence that spirits-made-flesh are a thing that can happen.<br /> <br /> There are less artless ways to point out that myths are myths.</div> </div> </div> </div>The popular theory about how Luna was able to take flesh concerns Claiming a fair maiden. Which is currently held in check by the proposition that Incarnae (much less a Celestine) can't be contained in such a limited form. But I digress, Satchel already expounded on the relevant trope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T17:39:55-07:00","id":125417,"title":"","content":"There's precedence for such beings existing in multiple ways at once, in both WOD books and real world mythologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T17:51:58-07:00","id":125423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=125408#post125408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The popular theory about how Luna was able to take flesh concerns Claiming a fair maiden. Which is currently held in check by the proposition that Incarnae (much less a Celestine) can't be contained in such a limited form.</div> </div> </div> </div>To point to further support, the opening story of the Lodge of the Storm's Eye in Lodges: The Splintered uses language that suggests the great spirit Yurgarath did something similar \u2014 &quot;[H]e watched over the tribes of men out of idle curiosity, going among them on two legs when he saw fit to veil his true nature in a covering of mortal flesh&quot; \u2014 and the second chapter of Predators notes that for the most part it's Jagglings and greater Gafflings who make up the majority of Ridden \u2014 &quot;Generally speaking [\u2026] Incarnae would actually be lessened by devoting their considerable power to a puny mortal shell.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-04-2014, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T19:01:26-07:00","id":125461,"title":"","content":"You probably can't reconstruct what could have happened in Pangaea based (solely) on the rules of the world post-Father Wolf, considering the whole mess that came with his death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T20:24:39-07:00","id":125504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=125461#post125461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You probably can't reconstruct what could have happened in Pangaea based (solely) on the rules of the world post-Father Wolf, considering the whole mess that came with his death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's the trope Satchel mentioned in action. I imagine in a world where the physical world and the shadow were one, spirits (even the most powerful ones) would not have so much difficulty taking physical form. That is, if pangea ever really existed. Believing in Pangea literally is a bit like believing in Eden literally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T20:36:47-07:00","id":125509,"title":"","content":"Pangaea literally as it's described, sure.<br /> But it does stand to reason that there were times when things were different.<br /> At the very least, if you go back far enough, to before there were humans and things with deep consciousness, everything was a reflection of everything else. A bird was a bird, had a reflection of a bird.<br /> But as humanity comes, they see a bird and dream of flying, of hope, concepts. They see a vulture eating a corpse, and now the vulture is a scavenger, disease-ridden. One guy walks down the plains and a bird shits on his head and he thinks they're awful things of bad luck, another catches one and has a great meal and birds are yummy.<br /> Even if it's a slow evolution of few things (prey, predator) to many (liberty, closeness to a higher place, freedom, etc), there'd be a definite change in the Shadow. And considering what we -do- know of the World of Darkness, it's likely their prehistory doesn't follow an exact parallel to ours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T21:30:50-07:00","id":125544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=125509#post125509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pangaea literally as it's described, sure.<br /> But it does stand to reason that there were times when things were different.<br /> At the very least, if you go back far enough, to before there were humans and things with deep consciousness, everything was a reflection of everything else. A bird was a bird, had a reflection of a bird.<br /> But as humanity comes, they see a bird and dream of flying, of hope, concepts. They see a vulture eating a corpse, and now the vulture is a scavenger, disease-ridden. One guy walks down the plains and a bird shits on his head and he thinks they're awful things of bad luck, another catches one and has a great meal and birds are yummy.<br /> Even if it's a slow evolution of few things (prey, predator) to many (liberty, closeness to a higher place, freedom, etc), there'd be a definite change in the Shadow. And considering what we -do- know of the World of Darkness, it's likely their prehistory doesn't follow an exact parallel to ours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. It's also interesting to note that there's a common theme throughout many WoD lines that there was once some sort of semi-mythical past wherein things used to be better, some catastrophe occurred and we ended up with the crapsack world that is WoD. You've got to think, there must be some grain of truth to all of these various sundering-type stories. You can't take any of them literally, but at the same time you can't ignore that pretty much everyone agrees the world used to be whole, something bad happened, and now it's broken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T22:31:03-07:00","id":125572,"title":"","content":"The fun thing about the whole &quot;semi-mythical past&quot; thing a few WoD games have going on in that the semi-mythical pasts were actually quite horrible places for everyone concerned. The World of Darkness doesn't do utopias.<br /> <br /> The myth of Pangaea isn't about an Eden that was lost due to a terrible mistake, it's about a flawed paradise that had to be brought down before it consumed the world. The story of Father Wolf is, at its core, a story of personal responsiblity \u2014 of a pack of werewolves making a terrible decision that nonetheless had to be made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T23:10:03-07:00","id":125588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=125572#post125572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The myth of Pangaea isn't about an Eden that was lost due to a terrible mistake, it's about a flawed paradise that had to be brought down before it consumed the world. The story of Father Wolf is, at its core, a story of personal responsiblity \u2014 of a pack of werewolves making a terrible decision that nonetheless had to be made.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The world might have been better off if you had never been born&quot; is another way to read common interpretations of the start of Urfarah's flagging health, I note, which speaks volumes about the species' sense of security.<br /> <br /> The stories the Ivory Claws tell about Luna, biased though they may be, provoke some thought concerning Her motivation for giving rise to a species whose birth and rearing would result in the weakening of their otherwise-immortal progenitor.<br /> <br /> I don't think of Eden. I think of the Nameless Empire. After factoring in the above stories and Papa Wolf's summation of the Uratha as the children of the Great Hunter and the Queen of Air and Darkness, I think of Mage's take on Camelot. With a little bit of thinking back to Voice of the Angel, I remember the mantra of the Machine.<br /> <br /> The erasure of an era-defining society as a catalyst for fundamental changes to the nature of the world in particular is a thing that shows up all over the place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T23:34:02-07:00","id":125596,"title":"","content":"It might be sorta fun to come up with a coherent-ish narrative where the Iremite sorcerers ascended the Celestial Ladder and struck a deal with Mother Moon ending up with the Primal Wild casting a Shadow across the World of Darkness, before being thrown into Duat. Probably nearly impossible, but still. (And I probably got the Mummy lore wrong.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T00:53:00-07:00","id":125624,"title":"","content":"Not worth the effort beyond a purely intellectual exercise, IMHO. The appeal I get from divergent mythologies is that very divergence, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T01:11:33-07:00","id":125631,"title":"","content":"It is possible-enough threads exist to weave your own tapestry, even though we're still digging out the skeleton's in the Mummy cosmology's closet.<br /> <br /> But it's also tremendously dull and unimportant to the time most of your games take place-even the earliest suggestions are beyond the point of care. The beginning isn't acutally important as an actual event, it's important as a idea.<br /> <br /> Well...Except for Irem. The doings of the Shan'iatu are still relevant to the world today, even if only mummies can do shit with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T03:39:34-07:00","id":125689,"title":"","content":"Oh, come now. This all isn't even touching on the fact it's so heavily cultural biased, and that other nations would not use the same Western culture mythos","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-05-2014, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T09:43:08-07:00","id":125887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=125689#post125689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, come now. This all isn't even touching on the fact it's so heavily cultural biased, and that other nations would not use the same Western culture mythos</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair? the sources from those tales are virtually immortal spirits. Biased as they may be due to an agenda and/or their inherent insanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:46:24-07:00","id":126016,"title":"","content":"^this. It may speak of a western animistic sorta theme to some, but the first profession was shamanism after all... (look up the magic man cave painting) so the idea of this spirit world mindset being the fore isn't all that crazy. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:52:47-07:00","id":126019,"title":"","content":"The most important takeaways from the myth are, to my mind,<br /> <br /> 1) the basic narrative framework of the game. The point of the Father Wolf myth is that it in part is what answers the question &quot;What do werewolves do?&quot; The story of Father Wolf gives you one possible approach; a potential structure to follow. Structure's good in a game, because it's giving you default story ideas that come easily to Storytellers. In this case, it's recreating Father Wolf's spirit hunts, and dealing with werewolves who also believe in this myth and hate you for the part your ancestors played in it.<br /> <br /> 2) The Father Wolf myth is also big on symbolism; a story of personal responsibility \u2014 of a pack of werewolves making a terrible decision that nonetheless had to be made, mirroring possible situations and outcomes in the lives of many Forsaken packs. In the World of Darkness, doing the right thing means that you're going to suffer, and this is reflected well in the Father Wolf myth. You have this flawed paradise that threatened to consume the world, and thus, had to be brought down; and you have the cowards who just didn't have the guts to act when necessity arose, and, due to their own moral failings, now seek to purge those who did the right thing from the face of the earth.<br /> <br /> 3) Antagonists that emphasize the primal feel of the game - things like the Spinner-Hag or the Plague-King or the Famine-Bringer that, by existing, not just suggest a possible truth behind the myth, they are also great antagonists. A werewolf game needs prey for the protagonists to hunt, and demon-gods from an age gone by fit the bill nicely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T15:17:34-07:00","id":129293,"title":"","content":"Nicely said Christian A , I am in total agreement to this . And all people as well who responded to the topic .<br /> Although there are some details to the whole matter . <br /> <br /> a) Luna supports the Forsaken as the good mother she is . Even a cruel one , not to completely forgive them rather than just soften her curse .<br /> <br /> b) The Sartha are pieces that struggle to come together by devouring each other (T2000-like) . In order to complete what ? become one ? so the legends of the ancient broken gods are true (spiner hug etc etc) . <br /> <br /> c) The Forsaken Totems speak about father wolf , not with details but they do , to remind them the mistakes of the past and the duty they have to fulfill the role of their father , or half father , or whatever .<br /> <br /> d) The forsaken took the role of the father wolf willingly or not , they know it because all their acts preserve the world , while when they become dull or when they fail to theor tasks , the world goes to the worst .<br /> <br /> e) The hate of the Pure , even though it is completely abnormal even for werewolves to go to the extreme and kill their own kind for some ancient hate even to the point of losing their souls ....eeerr spirits . I mean hold grudges , yes , but fanatical hate for an age long past ? Especially when the pure themselves took no mantle of balance perservation and world guarding like Father Wolf wore so many years ago . I mean if they loved their father so much why not try to look like him ? <br /> <br /> f) The kuruth effects in hisil , with father wolf's dying echo and stuff .<br /> <br /> g) All spirits hate the forsaken for killing ... umm .. their tyrant ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T17:51:09-07:00","id":129439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=129293#post129293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">g) All spirits hate the forsaken for killing ... umm .. their tyrant ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they hate the Forsaken for taking on his role. Also, for being creating a separation between the material world and the shadow. Back in Pangea (if it ever really existed) the spirits had no need to urge, or claim, or possess physical beings, or to worm their way through weak points in the gauntlet, because the spirit world and the physical world were one and the same. They could roam freely and do as they chose. They did have to fear Urfarah, but in retrospect, one apex predator and the whole world as their stomping ground was a lot better than being barred from the physical world and hunted by half a million of his children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T18:04:48-07:00","id":129454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=129293#post129293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a) Luna supports the Forsaken as the good mother she is . Even a cruel one , not to completely forgive them rather than just soften her curse .</div> </div> </div> </div>Or she's cleaning up her mess, or the Lunes are acting on their own, or the ability to weaken the curse of silver required that the curse of silver exist to begin with, or\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> b) The Sartha are pieces that struggle to come together by devouring each other (T2000-like) . In order to complete what ? become one ? so the legends of the ancient broken gods are true (spiner hug etc etc) . </div> </div> </div>They're consuming each other to become stronger, because they act like fleshy versions of spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> c) The Forsaken Totems speak about father wolf , not with details but they do , to remind them the mistakes of the past and the duty they have to fulfill the role of their father , or half father , or whatever . </div> </div> </div>They're talking to werewolves who know of the myth. It suits their purposes to keep mouthing the party line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> e) The hate of the Pure , even though it is completely abnormal even for werewolves to go to the extreme and kill their own kind for some ancient hate even to the point of losing their souls ....eeerr spirits . I mean hold grudges , yes , but fanatical hate for an age long past ? Especially when the pure themselves took no mantle of balance perservation and world guarding like Father Wolf wore so many years ago . I mean if they loved their father so much why not try to look like him ? </div> </div> </div>They've bound themselves to multiple gods who have been bound to werewolf-strength unreasoning hatred for generations upon generations, they draw more of their worldview from spirits than humans, spirits are incredibly vindictive, Urfarah's title is meaningless in a world without the Border Marches, and the Pure's softer stance on the divide between Shadow and Flesh amounts more to &quot;we have the right to enact whatever policies we can get through on the Shadow and spirits of whatever territory we can hold onto, but the rest of the world isn't our problem.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's a reason many of the Pure are essentially slaves to minor gods of the Shadow who've convinced a few werewolves to trade out their silver Renown brands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> g) All spirits hate the forsaken for killing ... umm .. their tyrant ? </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hey guys, we're horrifying abominations against the natural order, sired upon the mad goddess of a distant celestial object by that guy who keeps stopping you from getting all the neat stuff in the world of flesh but who you more or less respected for being strong enough to consistently do so. We just exploited a cosmological convergence and killed him in the cheatiest way imaginable because his getting weaker was letting you all get away with more stuff, and now that strange and terrifying goddess of night and madness has sent pieces of herself to empower us to do unspeakable harm to you and mitigate the consequences she levied on us for killing her babydaddy when she wasn't looking. Can we be friends?&quot;<br /> &quot;&lt;loud sibilant screeching faintly evocative of the phrase 'GET THE FUCK AWAY FROM US'&gt;&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T23:45:18-07:00","id":129666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=129293#post129293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">c) The Forsaken Totems speak about father wolf , not with details but they do , to remind them the mistakes of the past and the duty they have to fulfill the role of their father , or half father , or whatever .</div> </div> </div> </div>The Firstborn don't generally speak to the Forsaken. When they do, they give orders and commands while talking about duty and sacrifice and all.<br /> <br /> Some Ghost Wolves are pretty suspicious about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=129293#post129293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">d) The forsaken took the role of the father wolf willingly or not , they know it because all their acts preserve the world , while when they become dull or when they fail to theor tasks , the world goes to the worst .</div> </div> </div> </div>You change. You see the places where the wall between worlds is thin. You see the shadowy things that wiggle through. You see how they take mortal flesh and fuck up the world. Are you going to abase yourself before these things and take their side? Or are you going to attempt to hunt them down?<br /> <br /> Being a Forsaken isn't about emulating a wolf-god who might or might not have existed an apocalypse ago. It's about putting yourself into mortal danger so that your place is kept clean and the ones you love get to be safe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=129293#post129293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">e) The hate of the Pure , even though it is completely abnormal even for werewolves to go to the extreme and kill their own kind</div> </div> </div> </div>It's completely abnormal for humans to kill other humans. Yet they still do, every day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=129293#post129293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> for some ancient hate even to the point of losing their souls ....eeerr spirits . I mean hold grudges , yes , but fanatical hate for an age long past ? Especially when the pure themselves took no mantle of balance perservation and world guarding like Father Wolf wore so many years ago . I mean if they loved their father so much why not try to look like him ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about Father Wolf.<br /> <br /> You change. Your old life is destroyed. You are a mad, half-beast, half-man thing. Someone comes up to you and says &quot;Now that you're a monster, you have to join us and struggle to save the world. You'll bleed, you'll hurt, you'll lose your loved ones, and the world will not love you for your efforts, but you must because nobody else will.&quot; Or someone else says &quot;You think your life sucks now? Let me show you why your life sucks and how you can get even. Oh, did I mention these really powerful spirit-monsters are gonna give you kewl powerz?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Forsaken hunt dangerous spirits. Doing so puts them into mortal danger almost every day.<br /> <br /> The Pure don't quite have the moral fortitude to do so. That's why they choose the easy way out - they <i>serve </i>dangerous spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=129293#post129293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">g) All spirits hate the forsaken for killing ... umm .. their tyrant ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits don't hate you for killing their ... jailor? And taking on his mantle. If anything, they would be glad about you having killed Father Wolf.<br /> <br /> Spirits hate you because you're between them and the fulfillment of their highest aspirations, to enter the Flesh and to build their little kingdoms, possessing people, etc.<br /> <br /> Don't try to explain the status quo of the setting by using the Father Wolf myth. Father Wolf has been absent from the setting a very long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 05-10-2014, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T04:23:35-07:00","id":129783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=129666#post129666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Firstborn don't generally speak to the Forsaken. When they do, they give orders and commands while talking about duty and sacrifice and all.<br /> Some Ghost Wolves are pretty suspicious about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is quite interesting , totems being the grand manipulators , hmmmm .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=129666#post129666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't try to explain the status quo of the setting by using the Father Wolf myth. Father Wolf has been absent from the setting a very long time ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still the topic is about uratha origins and what might be true or false . Ths is still a part of the setting .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=129439#post129439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They did have to fear Urfarah, but in retrospect, one apex predator and the whole world as their stomping ground was a lot better than being barred from the physical world and hunted by half a million of his children.</div> </div> </div> </div>True !<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=129454#post129454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or she's cleaning up her mess, or the Lunes are acting on their own, or the ability to weaken the curse of silver required that the curse of silver exist to begin with, or\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed ...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=129454#post129454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're consuming each other to become stronger, because they act like fleshy versions of spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or become one again !<br /> <br /> <br /> Note: I tried a Pure capaign once with people who never played forsaken first , it seemed to them that the forsaken where the bad guys .<br /> <br /> That made me think the posibility that the firsaken's progenitors were indeed the bad guys !!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2194,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","user":"Furry","date":". 05-10-2014, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T04:32:28-07:00","id":129788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=129783#post129783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is quite interesting , totems being the grand manipulators , hmmmm .</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a nice idea that a few books such as Predators or The Rage or Tribes of the Moon hint at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/125314-uratha-origins-what-exactly-happened?p=129783#post129783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still the topic is about uratha origins and what might be true or false . Ths is still a part of the setting .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's ok, it still bears mention, though, that when assuming that the myth is the full and complete truth, you're moving a slight bit away from the official setting. In the official game, the motivations of the Forsaken, the Pure and the spirits can be explained by things that happen in the status quo of the setting, not by the Father Wolf myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T10:41:54-07:00","id":129985,"title":"","content":"It doesn't help that you get such a weird mix of obviously biased, &quot;This story is true...&quot; retellings and to-the-player/storyteller stuff that paints the picture of a strange prehistoric fantasy world where spider kings slaughter towns. Especially since it fits, considering the feudal nature of the spirit world.<br /> <br /> I like the myth, though. It works, gives some good motivation to descendants of the lord of the border marches, while being sufficiently detatched from things to appreciate a werewolf flat out disbelieving it and doing his own thing. There's kind of a Vimes vibe going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-10-2014, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T12:39:55-07:00","id":130078,"title":"","content":"So the conclusion is that everything is blurry and flux .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T12:46:04-07:00","id":130080,"title":"","content":"Nothing is true, everything is permitted...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/y_sEyky7NlY\" data-code=\"y_sEyky7NlY\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/y_sEyky7NlY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T12:59:39-07:00","id":130089,"title":"","content":"The myth is just that, a myth. The myth has answers to the big questions, but there are other myths, and the answers aren't necessarily true. It's all a matter of faith.<br /> <br /> Like, you know, in real life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","n